# Description: GET RESPONSE: fetch data waiting after a 61 XX "more data" status.
# Category: utilities
#
# WHAT THIS DOES
# When a card answers a command with status 61 XX it means: "I succeeded,
# and XX more bytes of response data are waiting for you." This script sends
# GET RESPONSE to collect those bytes. Run it immediately after you see a
# 61 XX status word, for example after a SELECT FILE. GET RESPONSE does not
# modify the card.
#
# THE COMMAND, BYTE BY BYTE
#   00     class byte: standard interindustry commands
#   C0     instruction: GET RESPONSE
#   00 00  P1-P2 must be zero for this command
#   20     Le: how many of the waiting bytes to request; 0x20 = 32. Replace
#          20 with the XX from the 61 XX status you received (Le 00 asks
#          for all 256 remaining bytes).
#
# WHAT YOU SHOULD SEE
#   The pending data followed by SW 90 00. If the card again answers 61 XX,
#   more data is still waiting: send GET RESPONSE again with the new XX.
#   SW 6C XX asks you to resend the previous command with Le = XX.
00 C0 00 00 20
